{[%cal Ge5a5,Ge5h5,Ge5e8,Ge5e1,Yd1h1,Yd1a1,Yd1d8] A paradox: a rook has exactly as many available squares on the edge as in the center. It therefore likes to remain farther back, since its mobility is unaffected and the center is dominated by minor pieces in the middlegame. This also helps explain why rooks are exchanged less often and why rook endings are the most common endings.}  *

